UID:hb100-w18-7-2027-02-20@tce-founder.ultra
DTSTAMP:20261018T222526Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270220T060000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270220T150000
SUMMARY:W18 · Art Loeb Trail traverse (9h00)
DESCRIPTION:Week 18 · Specific — mountain\, dark\, fuelled · 9\,200 ft 
 vert\\n\\n30.1 mi point-to-point\, ~9\,200 ft\, Davidson River to Camp Dan
 iel Boone. NOT a race — a big unsupported day\, and the largest single e
 ffort before the Heartbreaker. Budget 9 h\; it may take 11-12 and that is 
 fine. BAIL POINT: FS 816 at Black Balsam\, roughly two-thirds in and road-
 accessible — if you are more than 2 h over budget by Gloucester Gap (mil
 e 12.3)\, stop there instead. Needs a car shuttle at both ends. February o
 n the balds is genuinely exposed: this is the cold-kit test for Hellbender
 's 6\,684 ft summit.
CATEGORIES:LONG
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hb100-w18-8-2027-02-21@tce-founder.ultra
